*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* XATEST  -  ASSEMBLE ONE OF EACH MACRO AND CHECK THE BYTES           *
*                                                                     *
* THIS IS NOT MEANT TO RUN.  IT EXISTS SO THE ASSEMBLER LISTING CAN BE*
* COMPARED AGAINST KNOWN-GOOD ENCODINGS BEFORE ANY OF THESE MACROS IS *
* TRUSTED IN REAL CODE.  FIVE OF THE ENCODINGS BELOW HAVE ALREADY BEEN*
* EXECUTED SUCCESSFULLY UNDER HERCULES; THE REST COME FROM READING    *
* SOURCE, WHICH IS WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.                              *
*                                                                     *
*   GLOBAL MACLIB XALIB                                               *
*   ASSEMBLE XATEST (PRINT                                            *
*                                                                     *
* THEN READ XATEST LISTING AND COMPARE THE OBJECT COLUMN WITH THE     *
* EXPECTED VALUES IN THE COMMENTS.  THE BASE AND DISPLACEMENT HALFWORD*
* WILL DEPEND ON WHERE THE OPERANDS LAND, SO ONLY THE FIRST TWO BYTES *
* ARE FIXED -- BUT THOSE ARE THE ONES THAT DECIDE WHICH INSTRUCTION   *
* THE MACHINE EXECUTES.                                               *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
XATEST   CSECT
         BALR  R15,0
         USING *,R15
*
* R1 MUST HOLD X'0001' IN THE HIGH HALFWORD AND THE SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
* IN THE LOW BEFORE ANY OF THE SUBCHANNEL INSTRUCTIONS.  BITS 0-15
* MUST BE EXACTLY 0001, NOT MERELY NON-ZERO.
*
         L     R1,SSIDW
*
*        EXPECT                     INSTRUCTION
*        ------                     -----------
         STSCH SCHIB           *    B234  proven by execution
         MSCH  SCHIB           *    B232  proven by execution
         SSCH  ORB             *    B233  proven by execution
         TSCH  IRB             *    B235  proven by execution
* EXPECT B230 0000
         CSCH
* EXPECT B231 0000
         HSCH
* EXPECT B238 0000 -- OPCODE DISPUTED, SEE XAOPS
         RSCH
* EXPECT B237 0000
         SAL
         TPI   PARM            *    B236
         STCRW PARM            *    B239
*
         BSM   R1,0            *    0B10  proven by execution
         BSM   0,R4            *    0B04  proven by execution
         BASSM R14,R15         *    0CEF
*
* THESE NEED NO MACRO -- THE ASSEMBLER ALREADY KNOWS THEM, AND IF ANY
* OF THE FOUR FAILS TO ASSEMBLE THEN THE PROBLEM IS THE ASSEMBLER
* LEVEL RATHER THAN THE MACLIB.
*
         STOSM MASKSAVE,X'04'  *    AD04  DAT on
         STNSM MASKSAVE,X'FB'  *    ACFB  DAT off
         LCTL  1,1,CR1VAL      *    B711
         STCTL 0,15,CRSAVE     *    B60F
*
         BR    R14
*
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* OPERANDS.  THE ALIGNMENT RULES DIFFER WITHIN ONE SEQUENCE AND THE   *
* MACHINE ENFORCES EACH OF THEM SEPARATELY.                           *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         DS    0F
SSIDW    DC    X'00010000'          X'0001' || SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
CR1VAL   DC    X'00003001'          STO X'3000', STL 1 = 32 ENTRIES
PARM     DS    F
MASKSAVE DS    X
         DS    0F
CRSAVE   DS    16F                  STCTL 0,15 STORES ALL SIXTEEN
*
* ORB -- WORD ALIGNED.  THIRTY-TWO BYTES, NOT TWELVE: HERCULES FETCHES
* SIZEOF(ORB)-1 UNCONDITIONALLY WHATEVER THE EXTENSION BIT SAYS, SO A
* TWELVE-BYTE ORB AT THE END OF AN IMAGE TAKES AN ADDRESSING EXCEPTION
* ON A FETCH THE ARCHITECTURE SAYS NEVER HAPPENS.
*
         DS    0F
ORB      DC    X'00000000'          INTERRUPTION PARAMETER, YOUR TAG
         DC    X'00'                FLAG4: KEY 0 DISABLES CHANNEL KEY
*                                   CHECKING ENTIRELY
         DC    X'80'                FLAG5: F=1, FORMAT-1 CCWS
         DC    X'80'                LPM -- MUST BE 80.  SSCH TESTS
*                                   LPM AND PAM, AND PAM IS 80, SO 00
*                                   IS CC 3 RATHER THAN "ANY PATH"
         DC    X'00'                FLAG7
         DC    A(MYCCW)             CCW ADDRESS, BIT 0 MUST BE ZERO
         DC    5F'0'                PAD TO THIRTY-TWO
*
         DS    0F
SCHIB    DS    XL52                 STSCH STORES 52, MSCH READS 28
         DS    0F
IRB      DS    XL64                 TSCH STORES ALL 64
*
* THE CCW MUST BE ON A DOUBLEWORD BOUNDARY OR IT IS A CHANNEL PROGRAM
* CHECK -- A DIFFERENT RULE FROM THE ORB, SCHIB AND IRB, WHICH NEED
* ONLY A WORD.
*
         DS    0D
MYCCW    DC    X'09'                WRITE WITH AUTO CARRIER RETURN
         DC    X'20'                SLI, SUPPRESS INCORRECT LENGTH
         DC    AL2(L'MSG)
         DC    A(MSG)
MSG      DC    C'XATEST'
*
         LTORG
*
R0       EQU   0
R1       EQU   1
R2       EQU   2
R3       EQU   3
R4       EQU   4
R14      EQU   14
R15      EQU   15
         END
